    fix(frontend): name an answered-but-unusable 200 as its own failure state (ORD-0263)
    
    Both request channels discarded the fact that the origin answered: v8Request turned an
    unparseable body into null (so a later property read threw a TypeError, and the classifier
    filed it as a network failure), requestJson handed the document back as data and said
    nothing at all. The health probe only re-classifies when it fails, so a healthy 200 kept the
    wrong sentence on screen.
    
    Adds OriginResponseUnusableError carrying the measured status and content type, classifies it
    as ORIGIN_INVALID_RESPONSE on HTTP_RESPONSE/RUNTIME before any status or TypeError branch can
    absorb it, and lets the cached copy be offered there like it already is for the two adjacent
    states. The four earlier branches keep their behaviour.

